      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Exact nonequilibrium work relations gave statistical mechanics a powerful quantitative framework beyond equilibrium and have influenced theory and experiment across many systems.",
        "attribution": "Jarzynski's equality and Crooks's fluctuation theorem are distinct, closely connected contributions; Evans's earlier fluctuation relations are part of the intellectual foundation. The three listed names capture central strands, though the broader development involved others.",
