      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The theory of defect-mediated two-dimensional melting established a striking universal account of phase transitions driven by topological defects, a major achievement in statistical physics.",
        "attribution": "The central KTHNY framework is associated with these three theorists, whose complementary work developed the theory. Credit should reflect the shared and sequential nature of the contribution.",
        "maturity": "The framework has been studied and tested for decades, with enduring influence on two-dimensional materials and phase transitions.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Real systems can depart from the idealized transition sequence, so the scope of the original framework depends on material and conditions."
        ]
      }
    },
