      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Energy landscape theory recast protein folding as a physical problem of competing pathways and rugged landscapes, giving a powerful organizing framework for biological physics.",
        "attribution": "Dill, Wolynes, and Onuchic are central architects of the landscape perspective and its influential formulations. The broader folding field includes major experimental and theoretical contributions beyond this group.",
        "maturity": "The framework has guided research for decades and gained support from experiment and computation, though protein folding remains a diverse set of problems.",
