        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation and the quantum origin of cosmic structure offer a profound account of early-universe physics and connect quantum fluctuations to observable structure.",
        "attribution": "Guth and Linde were central to inflation's conception and development; Mukhanov made a foundational contribution to the theory of primordial perturbations. These are related advances with distinct roles.",
        "maturity": "The framework has been developed and tested against precision cosmological observations, but its detailed mechanism and unique empirical signatures remain unsettled.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Inflation has not been uniquely established over competing early-universe scenarios, and the identity of the inflaton remains unknown."
        ]
